{'symbol': 'AMP', 'date': '2019-10-01 22:30:00', 'title': 'Amfam, Inc. completed its acquisition of IDS Property Casualty Insurance Company from Ameriprise Financial, Inc. (NYSE:AMP).', 'text': 'Amfam, Inc. entered into a definitive agreement to acquire IDS Property Casualty Insurance Company from Ameriprise Financial, Inc. (NYSE:AMP) for $1.1 billion on April 1, 2019. The purchase price is subject to certain post-closing financial adjustments. IDS Property Casualty Insurance Company will become a subsidiary within the American Family Insurance group and operate under its existing name until a new name is identified and approved by regulators. All IDS Property employees along with it’s headquarter in De Pere, Wisconsin will be retained by American Family Insurance, parent company of Amfam. Current IDS Property customers will retain their policies with no change in coverage or service. The transaction is subject to regulatory approval and satisfaction of other customary closing conditions. The transaction expected to close in the second half of 2019. George Matsuzaka, Carlos Marque and Daniel Schleifman of Credit Suisse Securities (USA) LLC acted as financial advisors and Todd freed, Patrick Lewis and Christopher Ulery of Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP acted as legal advisors to Ameriprise in the transaction. Anne E. Ross, Thomas R. Hrdlick and Maureen C. Easton of Foley & Lardner acted as legal advisors and Seth Bair, Peter Houston, Dan Bank and Elizabeth Durkin of Keefe, Bruyette, & Woods, Inc. acted as financial advisors to American Family insurance company.\nAmfam, Inc. completed its acquisition of IDS Property Casualty Insurance Company from Ameriprise Financial, Inc. (NYSE:AMP) on October 1, 2019. After a payment to an affinity partner by Ameriprise, the net proceeds were approximately\xa0$1.035 billion, which is subject to certain post-closing financial adjustments. Jessie Stauffacher succeeds Tom Ealy as IDS president and chief executive officer.\xa0Tom Ealy is retiring from IDS but will continue as a consultant through year end. Sharena Ali was appointed to the new position of chief operating officer at IDS.\n'}
{'symbol': 'ABC', 'date': '2019-10-01 22:30:00', 'title': 'Karyopharm Therapeutics Inc. Selects AmerisourceBergen Corporation to Support XPOVIO', 'text': "AmerisourceBergen announced that it has been selected by Karyopharm Therapeutics Inc. (Karyopharm) to support XPOVIO(TM) (selinexor). AmerisourceBergen is providing a unified commercialization approach for XPOVIO(TM), which was approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) on July 3, 2019. XPOVIO(TM) is a nuclear export inhibitor indicated in combination with dexamethasone for the treatment of adult patients with relapsed or refractory multiple myeloma (RRMM) who have received at least four prior therapies and whose disease is refractory to at least two proteasome inhibitors, at least two immunomodulatory agents, and an anti-CD38 monoclonal antibody. In the United States, there are 32,000 new cases of multiple myeloma, a cancer of plasma cells, each year. There are approximately 130,000 patients living with multiple myeloma in the United States today. The blood cancer is characterized by disease-related symptoms, including fatigue or weakness, unusual bleeding or bruising, and bone pain or fractures.3 Patients who suffer from relapsed and refractory multiple myeloma have an average five to nine month survival rate depending on the number of prior lines of therapy.4 XPOVIO(TM) inhibits the function of a nuclear export protein called XPO1 and induces the accumulation of tumor suppressor proteins in the cell nucleus, leading to the selective death of cancer cells. AmerisourceBergen's established expertise in supporting rare disease treatments helps ensure that critical medications are safely delivered from manufacturers to patients every day. AmerisourceBergen is supporting XPOVIO(TM) through: Specialty distribution: ASD Healthcare, one of the nation's largest specialty pharmaceutical distributors servicing 95% of U.S. hospitals, as well as specialty pharmacies, hemophilia centers, home healthcare companies and retail pharmacies, handles distribution services. Oncology Supply provides specialty distribution to independent oncology practices nationwide; GPO contracting for community oncology: AmerisourceBergen provides GPO contracting, integrated dispensing solutions and expertise through ION Solutions, the largest physician service organization and group purchasing organization specializing in the support of independent, community oncology practices; Third-party logistics: ICS, a pharmaceutical third-party logistics provider with 925,000 square feet of managed warehouse space across four strategic locations, aims to increase supply chain efficiency and ensure commercial success for selinexor. ICS will support distribution to specialty pharmacies and distributors. ICS was engaged two years prior to commercialization to support API storage and preparation for launch; Dispensing: AmerisourceBergen's specialty pharmacy US Bioservices has more than two decades of experience supporting small patient populations and is dispensing XPOVIO(TM). The pharmacy also provides customized clinical care, focused on supporting adherence and patient outcomes. Physicians may submit prescriptions for selinexor to US Bioservices via phone (877.757.0667), fax (888.899.0067), ePrescribe or the MyPathpoint Prescriber Portal."}
{'symbol': 'ANTM', 'date': '2019-10-01 22:30:00', 'title': 'Anthem, Inc. Elects Ryan Schneider to Serve as an Independent Director and Member Audit Committee of the Board Effective Immediately', 'text': "Anthem, Inc. announced that on October 1, 2019, the Board of Directors of the company elected Ryan Schneider to serve as an independent director effective immediately, with a term expiring at the company's 2022 annual meeting of shareholders. The Board also appointed Mr. Schneider to the Audit Committee of the Board. Mr. Schneider, 49, is the Chief Executive Officer for Realogy Holdings Corporation."}
