{'symbol': 'MKC', 'date': '2019-10-01 22:30:00', 'title': 'McCormick & Company, Incorporated Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fiscal Year of 2019', 'text': 'McCormick & Company, Incorporated provided earnings guidance for the fiscal year of 2019. For the period, the company expects to grow sales compared to 2018 by 1% to 2%, which in constant currency is a 3% to 4% projected growth rate. Operating income in 2019 is expected to grow 8% to 9% from $891 million of operating income in 2018. McCormick increased its projected 2019 earnings per share to be in the range of $5.20 to $5.25 compared to $7.00 of earnings per share in 2018.'}
{'symbol': 'MCHP', 'date': '2019-10-01 22:30:00', 'title': 'Microchip Technology Incorporated Enters into Amendment No. 1 to Amended and Restated Credit Agreement', 'text': "On September 26, 2019, Microchip Technology Incorporated entered into amendment No. 1 to amended and restated credit agreement among the Subsidiary Guarantors party thereto, the lenders party thereto and JPMorgan Chase Bank, N.A., as Administrative Agent (the Administrative Agent), which amends that certain Amended and Restated Credit Agreement, May 29, 2018, by and among the company, the lenders from time to time party thereto and the Administrative Agent (as amended, restated, supplemented or otherwise modified from time to time, the Credit Agreement). The Amendment amended the Credit Agreement to, among other things, reduce the margin added to the interest rate on revolving loans under the Credit Agreement to 0.0% to 0.75% for base rate loans and 1.0% to 1.75% for LIBOR rate loans, in each case determined based on the Company's senior leverage ratio. In addition, the revolving loan commitments were reduced by $30.0 million."}
